# avoid.curated — the curated source of scripts/avoid.sh (spec §2.7 source 4, design §9.1,
# PLAN.md §5.5): names from the Lean course (lean-learn-0) that this course must not reuse.
#
# Names only, copied from the R lane's accepted names-only scan of the Lean learner
# checkout's EXERCISE files (orchestrator decision, DV5a): never from its solutions, its
# reference trees or its proofs. Future scans of the Lean course go through this file
# only: refresh it by a names-only read of the Lean course's exercise files and record
# the date here (PLAN.md §8 R13 proposes the integration lane of each R phase).
# Lean Q's spine identifiers beyond `Bin` are not yet recorded (no accepted scan names
# them); add them at the next refresh.
#
# Columns (tab-separated): name, kind, applies, origin.
#   kind    name  = a hit when an own declaration's key equals this name's key;
#           type  = also a hit when this name's key occurs as a word run of an own key
#                   (`Tree` in `TreeSize`);
#           never = a hit when this exact token occurs anywhere in an own file.
#   applies Q, R or QR: the track(s) whose declarations are checked against the name
#           (Lean R's names against R, Lean Q's against Q; waiver direction Lean→<track>).
# `type` is kept for distinctive type names (Tree, Expr, Instr, Vect, Monoid, Bin: PLAN.md
# §5.5's examples and the R lane's note on Instr); Lean's `Value` is a `name`, since as a
# word it would fire on every R key that says "value" (`bound_value`) without any transfer.
# Keys are normalized as avoid.sh normalizes declarations (camelCase and snake_case
# split into words, lower-cased, joined with `_`).
name	kind	applies	origin
size	name	R	Lean R01-R06 exercise files, names only (R lane scan 2026-10-07, R-author-notes §8)
